Provenance: original work, and this project's own implementation throughout. There
is no third-party code in it and no dependency beyond the platform: the AAudio
interface in `src/backend/aaudio.rs` is declared by hand against the NDK's own
header, and the C ABI in `include/gnaudio.h` is this project's own.

One exception, and it is headers rather than code: `alsa-plugin/include/alsa/`
carries alsa-lib's public headers, which are LGPL-2.1-or-later and unmodified. They
are vendored so the plugin builds without an external source tree, and they are the
same license as this project, so the terms above cover them unchanged. The ALSA
plugin SDK those headers define — the exported entry point's name, and the
`snd_pcm_ioplug_t` layout libasound fills — is likewise the requester's interface,
not this project's design.

Where a literal name is required by something that is not ours to rename — an
interface a host looks up by name, such as libasound's mangled plugin symbol — that
literal is the requester's, not this project's naming.
